{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/444507-ideas-thread-summer-and-winter-wedding","id":444507,"title":"Ideas thread: Summer and Winter Wedding","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-16T10:36:28-07:00","id":444507,"title":"Ideas thread: Summer and Winter Wedding","content":"Ideas ideas, ideas! Bring me your ideas!<br /> <br /> My player, the Queen of winter, is engaged to be wed to the Queen of Summer! The Winter Queen is rather new to the position, strangely thrust into the role by others, political savvy allies of hers. The Summer queen has reigned close to a decade now in her court. The two are indeed in love, but that does not mean everything will go smoothly!<br /> <br /> It's a large and well off Freehold, plenty of politics can happen and there are opportunities for money and favours to be thrown around.<br /> <br /> I'm curious to know any ideas anyone has for any of the following:<br /> - What strange events might occur at the ceremony?<br /> - What politics may happen in the background or lead up to the wedding?<br /> - What might the wedding itself be like, the joining of Summer and Winter?<br /> - What sorts of gifts would such a couple receive?<br /> - What would you serve at the reception?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anything beautiful, whimsical, savvy or sinister that comes to mind, throw it my way if you please. I'm trying to make sure this is as memorable as possible, and I'm always eager to see the fun things other minds cook up for scenarios like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2557-sloanathan","name":"Sloanathan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T07:18:41-07:00","id":447654,"title":"","content":"In France, we have an advertisement cofee which can be a good exemple for a ritual encounter in the Hedge between Summer and Winter court.<br /> <br /> And as a consequence of the Wedding... Maybe others seasons could be lessen, with effective Sping and Automne dropping to less than a month ?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T07:21:47-07:00","id":447660,"title":"","content":"wrong maneuver ... and i can't delete the wrong link... the good one : <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/__rX15fM2RE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/__rX15fM2RE\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/__rX15fM2RE\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/__rX15fM2RE </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T13:30:39-07:00","id":448169,"title":"","content":"3. Fire and Ice might be good thematics for the wedding itself, with a lot of focus on Water(as the result of the two Elements mixing). <br /> <br /> 2.And since Summer and Winter tend to have somewhat opposed views(in general, since I'm not sure how it works in your group's Freehold), so some from both sides might try to break it off because they're convinced it's a plot by the others to seize control. Winter more so, perhaps, because they tend to be the stealthier ones and because of the gap in experience and power you mentioned. <br /> <br /> 5. Not the most culinarily minded, but I'd generally focus on contrasts, especially between &quot;bland&quot; foods such as rice or tofu(representing how Winter blends into the background) and spicer ones like peppers(to represent &quot;fiery&quot; Summer). <br /> <br /> 1: One or both of the lucky couple's Keepers shows up. Not to claim them, but to congratulate them. They graciously offer some sort of blessing or gift, some mighty Token or power, and then leaves. Is it a trick, and the gift is some sort of horrific trap? Is the Keeper just doing something benevolent for once, a one time change of heart brought about by madness? Either way, the Changelings of the Freehold are likely running around like chickens with their heads cut off. <br /> <br /> 4: Speaking of gifts, here are some ideas for what it might be. If it's a Token, it might be something like a wreath that, if hung on the door of a room where a couple lay together(not even necessarily sexually!) the couple will produce children, regardless of anything that would prevent this. Another option might be a set of lockets that allow them to see the world from each other's senses and teleport to the other's side when they're needed. As for less concrete gifts, maybe they're blessed to be immortal and unaging so long as they love each other, or maybe things will now just go remarkably well for them so long as they stay faithful. Not sure about gifts for the Winter Queen(maybe a CD containing the Frozen soundtrack?), but for Summer, weapons and armor are always in style!<br /> <br /> Hope this might help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T09:42:05-07:00","id":454493,"title":"","content":"Exchanging of tactics between the two parties. The summer court learns hit and run guerrilla warfare from the winter court, while the winter court learn just how powerful their Contracts actually are from the summer court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}